<title>USA: TABLE - Federal Express sells $250 mln bonds.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Federal Express sells $250 mln bonds.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Federal Express Corp was priced on Monday via lead manager Morgan Stanley, Dean Witter, Discover &amp; Co, according to a syndicate official.</p>
<p>Federal Express is a leading express transporation</p>
<p>company, delivering documents and packages.</p>
<p>BORROWER FEDERAL EXPRESS CORP</p>
<p>AMT $250 MLN	 COUPON 7.60 PCT   MATURITY 7/1/2097</p>
<p>TYPE BONDS	   ISS PRICE 99.735  FIRST PAY DATE 1/1/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S BAA2  YIELD 7.62 PCT    PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P BBB	 SPREAD 103 BPS    CALLABLE  NO</p>
<p>((U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678 ))</p>
</text>
